{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"HANDOFF STATE (2026-11-11 16:20 PST, session 3d705fec)\n\n**Status:** CLOSED through the completion gate, class `preexisting`. All 3 acceptance-criteria boxes are ticked. AC2 and AC3 are tagged `[non-codebase]` with provenance lines, validated by `provenance_gaps`.\n\n**Root cause, with evidence:**\n- On 2026-09-03 01:36:18 UTC, a stranded `objects/maintenance.lock` was left behind. Git never expires that lock, and while it exists, `git maintenance run --auto` exits 0 and does nothing. This was reproduced on git 2.47.3 inside the container. rebar's explicit post-write step was therefore a silent no-op for about 10 weeks.\n- How the lock was stranded:\n  - `git fetch` and `git merge` start a foreground `maintenance run --auto` themselves. rebar suppressed this on commits but not on bounded sync/push fetches or merges.\n  - On this store that run is a full gc: a full repack took 605.6 s, and `gc --auto` took 133.9 s. A rebar timeout SIGKILLs only the parent, so the orphaned gc kept running outside the write lock. This was observed live, adopted by the container's PID 1.\n  - A hard kill during that run left the lock in place.\n\n**Production repair (11:25–11:39 PST):**\n- Backed up the gitdir to `/var/lib/rebar/backups/mcp-tickets-gitdir-20261111T192528Z` (12 GB, standalone; refs verified identical).\n- Under rebar's write lock: removed the stale lock, `gc.pid` and 12 stale `.keep` files, then ran `repack -a -d -l`.\n- `fsck --connectivity-only` exited 0, and refs were unchanged.\n- The backup is still on disk; delete it at the operator's discretion. The root disk is 55% used.\n\n**Before and after:**\n\n| Measure | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Loose objects | 78,737 | 4–336 in steady state |\n| Packs | 235 | 2–4 |\n| Store-wide position walk | 427.5 s | 220–232 s (limit 300 s) |\n| Per-ticket path walk | 105–117 s | 23–28 s |\n| `log --name-only -n 5000` | 21–33 s | 2.9–4.1 s |\n\n**Durable fix:**\n- Gerrit change 3351, merged as 334295da063a5840f17d689583337dbbd1587a33. It is deployed in release 0.15.1, container image aa1e294.\n- Bounded git children carry `maintenance.auto=false` and `gc.auto=0`, as does the container's start-up fetch.\n- The explicit step runs only the incremental tasks: commit-graph, loose-objects and incremental-repack.\n- A timed-out step is reaped as a process group, SIGTERM first.\n- No config key, env var or flag was added, and there is no `mechanism-ok` marker.\n\n**Follow-up bugs (all linked discovered_from):**\n- `saccharine-unwise-barnacle`: recover from a stale `maintenance.lock`. Needs a lock-mechanism decision.\n- `idle-ammoniacal-axisdeer`: group-reap the other bounded git calls, which leave `.keep` files and orphaned children.\n- `successive-deceptive-xiphias`: no path now prunes unreachable objects or expires reflogs; two docs are stale.\n\n**Pending decisions:** none for this ticket."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794442639333147995,"uuid":"327cda73-63f8-408f-9e81-00369b3a9b41"}